<title>USA: CFTC backs CME's Taiwan stock index futures plan.</title>
<headline>CFTC backs CME's Taiwan stock index futures plan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Futures Trading Commission said Wednesday it had approved the applications of the Chicago Mercantile Exchange for designation as a contract market in Dow Jones Taiwan Stock Index futures and futures option contracts.</p>
<p>The Dow Jones Taiwan Stock Index was developed to be representative of the market for Taiwan stocks that are readily accessible to investors worldwide. The index is a capitalization-based index of 113 highly capitalized and actively traded stocks listed on the Taiwan Stock Exchange.</p>
</text>
